//? Title: Xception: Linear Separable Filters in Full-Depth Residual Flows
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Spatial filtering and cross-channel mixing need not use one large dense kernel. Xception
separates these operations and arranges them in residual flows. We test the activation order
on signed data, verify all eight middle blocks and separate batch-normalisation state, then
show the complete compact-model tensor Adam loop on cached CIFAR-10 images.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.2_classic_architectures/xception.cpp`.

> The method

A 3×3 depthwise kernel D filters each input channel independently, then a 1×1 pointwise
matrix P mixes channels. With depth multiplier one, the effective dense kernel is

$$
K_{u,v,c,o}=D_{u,v,c}P_{c,o}.
$$
\alttext(The spatial kernel for one input channel is shared up to the pointwise output-channel mixing coefficient.)

Weights and MACs per spatial location become 9 Cin+Cin Cout rather than 9 Cin Cout.
This factorisation restricts each input channel's space-to-output kernel rank. Crucially,
Xception places no activation or BN between D and P: batch normalisation follows the
complete separable operation. Inserting ReLU between them prevents negative spatial
responses from reaching the channel mixer. An identity depthwise kernel and pointwise
weight -2 give y=-2x/sqrt(1.001) for inference BN with unit variance/gamma and zero mean/beta.
Its input derivative is constant even where x is negative. The signed fixture checks this
formula and the different extra-ReLU output.

The entry flow has two ordinary convolutions and three downsampling residual blocks. Eight
middle blocks each contain three preactivated separable convolutions. Exit flow downsamples,
then applies two postactivated separable convolutions before global averaging and a linear
classifier. The first entry block omits its leading ReLU. Skip projections omit ReLU. Every
separable operation learns BN gamma/beta; there is no dropout, label smoothing or auxiliary head.
The full 299-pixel, 1000-class model has 22855952 learnable scalars and 54528 moving-statistic
scalars, ending at 10×10×2048. The report instantiates that full forward graph without
backward storage, then checks gradients on a width-scaled graph retaining every block.

The library uses He initialization for ordinary convolutions, Glorot for separable filters,
and its fused-BN convention: batch variance normalises training output, while unbiased
variance updates the moving average. This last detail need not match Keras moving-variance
updates exactly. Moving statistics are separate state and must be saved with the parameters.

The compact fit uses quarter widths, 71-pixel bilinear inputs, BN momentum .9, 128 fitting,
64 validation and 64 official-test rows. Twenty epochs use batch eight, Adam(.001), an explicit
kernel penalty .0001/2, and independent padded crops/flips. Validation selects both parameter
and moving-state checkpoints; a final test pass uses inference moments. The cached-data
experiment is bounded for CPU execution and does not reproduce an ImageNet benchmark.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/xception_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/xception_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/xception_concept.tikz > build/xception_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/xception_concept.svg build/xception_concept.dvi > build/xception_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
